B.afa=s([B.No],t.F)
B.NS=new A.ez("bodyplan_mermaid","Mermaid","","Reduce your speed by 2. Moving through water doesn't cost extra movement. Gain {3 * Vitality} bonus Health and +1/+2 range on Attacks.","{Half Level} times per story, lure all characters that can hear you to your location. Your voice will only lure them for a short time, or till they are harmed.",B.afa,B.iJ)
B.N8=new A.ep("Flights","{Half Level}",!0)
B.agH=s([B.N8],t.F)
B.NT=new A.ez("bodyplan_winged","Flying","","You have -1 speed when not flying. You may start any situation already concentrating on natural flight.\n\nNatural Flight: [Reaction] During your Turn, spend your reaction and begin concentrating on natural flight. While concentrating, you gain 1 bonus speed, you dash instead of moving, and may fly vertically while moving. You must be in a free space on the ground to use abilities, weapon attacks, or at the end of your turn. You may concentrate on this in addition to other effects. Make only 1 concentration check for all the effects.\n\nIf you are knocked prone, your flight ends. Standing from prone still requires movement, and you may not fly until you are standing.","{Half Level} times per story, you can fly out of any scene or fly into any scene containing a party member. If anyone asks how you got there you must explain.",B.agH,B.iJ)
B.Nj=new A.ep("Bounces","{Level}",!0)
B.agO=s([B.Nj],t.F)
B.NY=new A.ez("bodyplan_bouncing","Bouncing","","Your movement is inconsistent and difficult to predict. Your movement doesn't provoke attacks and you may move through other creatures' spaces. At the end of your turn, choose a random direction and dash {1d6 /2} spaces in that direction. This counts as forced movement for colliding with terrain or being thrown into a pit.","{Level} times per story, after succeeding a Str, Dex, or Vit defense, you begin to bounce chaotically, preventing anyone from grabbing hold of you for a minute.",B.agO,B.iJ)
B.Nl=new A.ep("Squeezes","{Level}",!0)
B.afJ=s([B.Nl],t.F)
B.NE=new A.eU("swarm_damage","Biting Swarm","At the end of your turn, deal {Half Level d6} damage to enemies in your spaces.","",B.cV)
B.NI=new A.eU("swarm_heal","Mending Swarm","At the end of your turn, heal allies in your spaces {Half Level d6}.","",B.cV)
B.NH=new A.eU("swarm_shield","Sheltering Swarm","At the end of your turn, give allies in your spaces {Half Level d6} shield.","",B.cV)
B.acj=s([B.NE,B.NI,B.NH],t.CT)
B.NX=new A.ez("bodyplan_swarm","Swarm","","Increase your size by 1. You cannot be flanked and don't benefit from flanking. You automatically succeed checks to escape grapple. Creatures may occupy your spaces and your spaces count as free spaces for abilities. You may move through enemies' spaces, and enemies may move through you.\nIf two or more swarms overlap, at the end of any creature's turn who is inside of the overlap, including the swarms, they must succeed a Str defense or take {Level d6} Bludgeoning damage.","{Level} times per story, you can squeeze through a door, window, through any seal or any gap.",B.afJ,B.acj)
B.Nd=new A.ep("Wall Bursts","{Level /3}",!0)
B.ahS=s([B.Nd],t.F)
B.ND=new A.eU("vehicle_armored_transport","Armored Transport","You resist damage caused by attacks targeting allies riding you. [Reaction] After an ally becomes adjacent to you, you may spend your reaction to have them start riding you, and move into your space wherever you choose.","{Level /3} times per story, you may suddenly enter the scene by bursting through a wall.",B.ahS)
B.Nm=new A.ep("Burnouts","{Half Level}",!0)
B.afw=s([B.Nm],t.F)
B.NQ=new A.eU("vehicle_race_tires","Race Tires","Gain +2 speed.","{Half Level} times per story, you may flee the scene at high speed. People may give chase but you still burn rubber out.",B.afw)
B.Nq=new A.ep("Overruns","{Half Level}",!0)
B.abw=s([B.Nq],t.F)
B.NL=new A.eU("vehicle_treads","Treads","Ignore difficult terrain. You resist damage from collision regardless of success.","{Half Level} times per story, you may go up and over anything. If it cannot support your weight it is crushed underneath you without damaging you.",B.abw)
B.Nt=new A.ep("Pulls","{Half Level}",!0)
B.afl=s([B.Nt],t.F)
B.NK=new A.eU("vehicle_winch","Winch","Winch: [Reaction] During an ally's turn, move up to {Level} in a line without provoking attacks. You may do this when prone, but you take {Half Vitality d6} damage.\nHook: [Reaction] During an ally's turn, make a Melee Attack vs Dex targeting one enemy range {1 + Half Level}. On success, deal {Half Level d6} damage and pull the target up to {Half Level + 1} spaces. You may target allies but they take only {1d6} damage.","{Half Level} times per story, you may pull anyone you see to you.",B.afl)
B.NM=new A.eU("vehicle_forklift","Forklift","When you succeed on an attack against an adjacent enemy, you may lift the target until the start of your next turn. While lifted, the target is restrained, doesn't provoke attacks, and remains adjacent whenever you move, dash, or teleport.","",B.cV)
B.NP=new A.eU("vehicle_flying","Flying","Same as the Flying body plan: you have -1 speed when not flying and may use Natural Flight.","",B.cV)
B.afG=s([B.ND,B.NQ,B.NL,B.NK,B.NM,B.NP],t.CT)
B.NU=new A.ez("bodyplan_vehicle","Vehicle","","Gain +2 speed. You cannot climb. Forced movement targeting you is halved but damage from being forced into terrain is tripled.\nProne: When you are knocked prone, you cannot move nor dash, nor can you end the prone effect. Adjacent allies may spend a [Reaction] or [Action] to remove your prone.\nRiding: Adjacent allies may ride you, as long as at least 1 of their spaces can fit in your space, and that space doesn't contain another ally. For every space worth of ally unable to fit, reduce your speed by 1. While riding, players are prone, they may still be targeted for attacks, and they resist all damage and you take an equal amount of damage as they do if you were not also targeted by the attack. To begin riding and to stop riding players must pay the cost to stand from prone. Hexapod allies aren't damaged for becoming prone because of riding, and stop riding by spending 1 movement point.\nCollision: [Reaction] During your turn, you may move through an enemy who is a smaller size than you. Make a Status Check vs Str. On Success, deal {Vitality d12} Bludgeoning damage to you and the target and the target is knocked prone. On Problems, you take {Vitality d6} damage or are knocked prone.","",B.cV,B.afG)
B.NN=new A.eU("parts_universal","Universal"," Any of your allies may be your host, you can use a [Action] to move from your current host to a target ally. When an ally moves within {Half Level} spaces of you, you may spend your [Reaction] to move from your current host to that ally.","",B.cV)
B.NJ=new A.eU("parts_specific","Specific","You can only have a specific character be your host. At the end of your turn and your host turn, you and your host may give each other Shield and Health. During your turn, you may force your host to move up to {Half your speed}, this movement does provoke attacks. Whenever you or your host heals or gains shields you may give some or all of it to the other.","",B.cV)
B.acW=s([B.NN,B.NJ],t.CT)
B.NW=new A.ez("bodyplan_parts","Parts","Your body is a part of another character\u2019s body. You are connected to your host and cannot be separated from each other. Effects that move, dash, teleport, slow, or restrain your host also apply to you and vise versa.You may not use movement points. When you take the [run] action, you may force your host to move up to your speed and this movement can provoke attacks. When you take the [Retreat] action, you may force your host to move half your speed without provoking attacks. When your host doesn\u2019t provoke attacks of opportunity, you also avoid attacks of opportunity. For each size you are more than your host, reduce their speed by 1. If you are smaller or larger than your host, you may reposition yourself relative to your host during your turn so that you are within at least 1 of their spaces. When you die, you must run a generic body with no combat features from spawn to a space adjacent to your host to respond in your body. When your host dies, you are stuck attached to their body until your host moves to space adjacent to you and uses an object interaction to pick you up. When you pick this, choose between being Universal, or Specific.","","",B.cV,B.acW)
